<section class="ex-note" id="definition">
<h2>1. Definition &amp; Classification（定義與分類）</h2>
<ul>
<li>Perforating disorders：以 <strong>transepidermal elimination</strong>（經表皮排除）dermal connective tissue 成分為特徵的一群疾病。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>可能是 familial 或 acquired systemic conditions（如 chronic renal failure、diabetes mellitus）的主要表現；也可能是其他原發皮膚病的次要成分（secondary perforating disorders，Table 71-1）。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>Rare familial primary perforating disorders 通常在 childhood 發病：排出 collagen 者為 <strong>reactive perforating collagenosis（RPC）</strong>，排出 elastic fibers 者為 <strong>elastosis perforans serpiginosa（EPS）</strong>。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>類似的 adult-onset nonfamilial／acquired 病灶<mark data-q="109-28">最常與 chronic kidney disease 及 diabetes mellitus 相關</mark>。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>過去文獻歸納出 4 個 adult-onset acquired primary perforating disorders：<strong>Kyrle disease（KD）</strong>、<strong>acquired perforating collagenosis（APC）</strong>、<strong>perforating folliculitis（PF）</strong>、<strong>acquired elastosis perforans serpiginosa（AEPS）</strong>。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>後續研究發現這些疾病相似處多於差異，同一病人不同病灶的排出物（collagen、elastin fibers、fibrin）組成不一，因此有些作者主張合稱 <strong>acquired perforating dermatosis（APD）</strong>；統一名稱受到鼓勵，但了解 4 種型別的臨床與病理表現仍有助於理解疾病光譜及可能的系統性疾病關聯。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
</ul>
<table class="ex-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Secondary perforating disorders（Table 71-1）</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Hematomas；perforating calcinosis cutis；gout（urate crystals）；papular mucinosis（mucin）；perforating pseudoxanthoma elasticum；granuloma annulare；necrobiosis lipoidica；rheumatoid nodule；sarcoidosis；foreign body（silica、wood splinter、glass、metal）；infection（chromomycosis、leprosy）；tumor cells（melanoma、pilomatrixoma、epithelioid sarcoma）</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p class="ex-cite">Table 71-1，p.1204。</p>
<ul>
<li>APD 的同義詞（Table 71-2）包括：acquired reactive perforating collagenosis、hyperkeratosis follicularis et parafollicularis in cutem penetrans、hyperkeratosis penetrans、keratosis follicularis serpiginosa、Kyrle disease、Kyrle-like lesions、perforating disorder、perforating folliculitis、perforating folliculitis of hemodialysis、reactive perforating collagenosis of diabetes mellitus and renal failure、uremic follicular hyperkeratosis。<span class="ex-ref">p.1204</span></li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="ex-note" id="clinical">
<h2>2. Clinical Features（臨床表現）</h2>
<h3>Acquired perforating dermatosis（APD）</h3>
<ul>
<li>APD 是 adult-onset acquired perforating disease 的 umbrella designation，涵蓋 KD、APC、PF、AEPS；其中 AEPS 的臨床表現與相關疾病較有特色。沒有確立的地理或明確種族好發。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>典型病灶：round、umbilicated、skin-colored、erythematous 或 hyperpigmented 的 papules 與 nodules，中央有 <strong>crust 或 keratotic plug</strong>；主要在四肢 extensor surfaces 與軀幹（APC、KD）。較少侵犯臉或頭皮。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>中央 keratotic core 是<strong>最具特異性的臨床表現</strong>，但偶爾被病人挖掉，只留下淺 crater。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li><strong>Mucous membranes are spared</strong>（黏膜不受侵犯）。罕見情況可見 purple annular plaques，或 pustules 混雜 papules。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>搔抓可造成 koebnerization，在抓痕處出現線狀 umbilicated papules；有些病灶可呈 follicular-based 分布且 Koebner response 很少（perforating folliculitis）。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>曾有報告病灶疼痛與搔癢，程度從 mild 到 severe and intractable。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>Elastosis perforans serpiginosa（familial 或 acquired）</h3>
<ul>
<li>Papules 排成 <strong>serpiginous configuration</strong>，常有 central atrophy；通常侷限於身體 1 個區域，如 neck、trunk 或 extremities。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>病灶常無症狀，只偶爾出現 koebnerization。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>男性約為女性的 <strong class="ex-n">nearly 4 times</strong>；familial form 報告為 <strong>autosomal dominant</strong>。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>Reactive perforating collagenosis（familial）</h3>
<ul>
<li>Extremely rare familial disorder，最常在 early childhood 發病，男女比例相等；autosomal dominant 與 recessive 都有報告。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203</span></li>
<li>與 KD、APC 類似，在 superficial trauma 後於上、下肢（偶爾臉部）出現小 keratotic papules；此型的 <strong>koebnerization response 最強</strong>。<span class="ex-ref">p.1203–1205</span></li>
</ul>
<table class="ex-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Kyrle disease／APC</th><th scope="col">Perforating folliculitis</th><th scope="col">AEPS</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Age of onset</td><td>4th decade（average）</td><td>3rd decade（average）</td><td>2nd decade（average）</td></tr>
<tr><td>Site</td><td>Extensor lower and upper extremities；head、neck、trunk</td><td>Hair-bearing portions of extremities</td><td>Nape of neck；upper extremities；face；lower extremities</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cutaneous findings</td><td>Round、umbilicated、skin-colored、erythematous 或 hyperpigmented papules／nodules，中央 crust 或 keratotic plug</td><td>類似 KD／APC，但呈 follicular distribution，central crusting 程度不一</td><td>Papules in serpiginous configuration with central atrophy</td></tr>
